--   Let $G$ be finite and nonempty with decidable equality, and let a bounded source-full coarse-target schedule have parameters $k,r$, an initial complexity-bound array, a natural growth function, and a scale floor. For every initial ordered partition complex whose partition complexities satisfy that array at every rank and face, there exists a certificate for the schedule and initial complex.
